m.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/forem/forem","homepage":"https://forem.com","size":1725259,"stargazers_count":22543,"watchers_count":22543,"language":"Ruby","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":4153,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":555,"license":{"key":"agpl-3.0","name":"GNU Affero General Public License v3.0","spdx_id":"AGPL-3.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/agpl-3.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTE="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["community","discussion","feedback","hacktoberfest","open-source","rails","ruby"],"visibility":"public","forks":4153,"open_issues":555,"watchers":22543,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/forem/forem/pulls/16517","html_url":"https://github.com/forem/forem/pull/16517","diff_url":"https://github.com/forem/forem/pull/16517.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/forem/forem/pull/16517.patch","merged_at":"2022-02-22T15:22:06Z"},"body":"## What type of PR is this? (check all applicable)\r\n\r\n- [ ] Refactor\r\n- [ ] Feature\r\n- [x] Bug Fix\r\n- [ ] Optimization\r\n- [ ] Documentation Update\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\nFixes several RSS feed validity issues and makes improvements to the Articles RSS Feed based on [The W3 Validator recommendations](https://validator.w3.org/feed/).\r\n\r\n1. Remove the `<author>` tag from the main `<channel>` tag.\r\n2. Update `<item>` `<author>` tags to be RFC 2822-compliant emails (e.g. \"bob@bob.com (Bob Bobberson)\")  **QUESTION ON THIS**: Is this OK to display people's email addresses?  I couldn't figure out how to query the \"show/hide my email\" checkbox.\r\n3. Make feed image title and url match feed title and url.\r\n4. (And this was probably the biggest change) Remove relative anchor links from article bodies within the `<description>` tags by implementing a new Feed Scrubber\r\n5. Add an `<atom:link rel=\"self\">` tag.\r\n6. Set the content type to `text/xml` (this is apparently a topic where [people have *thoughts*.](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/595616/what-is-the-correct-mime-type-to-use-for-an-rss-feed)\r\n7. Reworded some of the `<title>` and `<description`> content to make them more useful(?).  **FEEDBACK NEEDED**: This is a pretty subjective change.  Let me know if it's OK or if we need to rework any of the wordings.\r\n\r\nI also refactored a bit to make it clear within the builder how the four different kinds of feed (user, tag, latest, and default) were different.\r\n\r\n## Related Tickets & Documents\r\n\r\n#16418 \r\n\r\n## QA Instructions, Screenshots, Recordings\r\n\r\n1. Navigate to /feed/tag/javascript\r\n2. View source (since changing content-type to `text/xml` makes some browsers recognize, parse, and change things like `&lt;` to `<`).\r\n3. Copy the result into the [W3C Feed Validator](https://validator.w3.org/feed/).\r\n\r\n![Screenshot of a happy validator.](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/14909201/153282856-c517035e-0b90-4a78-bd53-c99edda07e1f.png)\r\n\r\n## Added/updated tests?\r\n\r\n- [ ] Yes\r\n- [X] No, and this is why: No tests present for this RSS Builder prior\r\n- [ ] I need help with writing tests\r\n\r\n## [optional] What gif best describes this PR or how it makes you feel?\r\n\r\n![Bachelorette candidate saying, \"It feels good to be validated.\"](https://media.giphy.com/media/OWtpNt0fbvwLeKbHcB/giphy.gif)\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/forem/forem/issues/16517/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/forem/forem/issues/16517/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":6118886324,"node_id":"REFE_lADOBGPKJs5D